{"Title":"An Act clarifying the duties of the adjutant general","BillNumber":"S2362","DocketNumber":"SD2001","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"JCV0","Name":"John C. Velis","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JCV0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T11:42:02.16"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"JCV0","Name":"John C. Velis","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JCV0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T11:42:02.16"},{"Id":"N_C0","Name":"Nick Collins","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/N_C0","ResponseDate":"2023-10-25T12:43:20.9066667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2362/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Velis, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 2362) of John C. Velis for legislation to clarify the duties of the adjutant general.  Veterans and Federal Affairs.","DocumentText":"\tSection 15(b) of Chapter 33 of the General Laws, as so appearing in the 2022 Official Edition, is hereby amended by inserting the following sentence:- The adjutant general shall have command of all of the militias of the Commonwealth.  \r\n\tSection 15(b) of Chapter 33 of the General Laws is hereby amended by striking the following:- ; provided, however, that the adjutant general shall not personally exercise command of troops.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J31","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J31"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}